content.text:
The fault is in ts-travel2-service, and its failures reach users through route-plan and travel-plan.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel2-service",
      "fault_kind": "application_exception",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) err, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.5)/1e6,1) p50ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel2-service' AND span_name IN ('GET /api/v1/travel2service/routes/{tripId}','Travel2Controller.getRouteByTripId') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Every travel2 GET /routes/{tripId} server span (3497) and its controller span errored in about 3 ms."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, left(message,160) m, count(*) c FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-travel2-service' AND level='SEVERE' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "ts-travel2-service logged 3497 SEVERE 'Unexpected error' RuntimeException exceptions from the dispatcher servlet."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) err FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel2-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Travel2's outgoing client calls show zero errors, so the failure originates inside travel2 itself rather than in its callees."}
      ]
    }
  ],
